{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_actor", "label": "Actor base class", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The foundational primitive: everything else in the framework \u2014 supervision, sharding, persistence, HTTP, brokers \u2014 builds on it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_privatemailbox", "label": "Private mailbox and single-threaded loop", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two messages never run concurrently for the same actor, so fields are read and mutated without locks or atomics and state is reasoned about like a single-threaded program."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_actorref", "label": "ActorRef handle", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A thin location-transparent handle, not the instance \u2014 refs cross the cluster and can be stored and passed on, while the underlying class is never visible."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_lifecyclehooks", "label": "Actor lifecycle hooks", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "preStart, postStop, preRestart and postRestart all default to no-op and may return a promise the framework awaits before the next phase; a throw in preStart escalates to the supervisor."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_displayname", "label": "Actor.displayName()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Resolved on every record rather than captured once, so it may be derived from state and follows a restart. Added to the line rather than substituted for the path; a throw falls back to the path."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_contextreferences", "label": "Context references (self, sender, system, log, context)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_thiscluster", "label": "this.cluster and context.cluster", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "this.cluster throws when the system never joined one, assuming code reaching for it already knows it is clustered; context.cluster answers None instead. Both read through on every access, so an actor already running when the join completes picks it up."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_asynconreceive", "label": "Async onReceive", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The framework awaits the returned promise before pulling the next message, so per-actor serialization is guaranteed. The trade-off is throughput \u2014 the usual fix is spawning a child per long-running task."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_children", "label": "Child actors", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Children are tied to the parent lifecycle: when the parent stops, all children stop first and postStop runs bottom-up."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_senderoption", "label": "sender is an Option, not an ActorRef", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Not every message has a sender \u2014 a tell from outside the actor world attaches None \u2014 so an unconditional sender.tell would throw on those messages."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_contextreferences", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_system_actorsystem", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_actor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_privatemailbox", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_actor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_actorref", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_actor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_lifecyclehooks", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_acto